<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20063" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gypsĕus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		gypsum. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Of gypsum</i> (post-class.),
				<i><span class="en">Spart. Sever. 22, § 3</span></i>.
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Covered</i> or <i>plastered with
				gypsum</i>, = gypsatus: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">facies (mulierum),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hier. Ep. 38, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
